---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import profile from '../../data/profile.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="People — VIOT Research" page="about" description="Principal Investigator profile and complete documentation record.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">People</p>
      <h1>Principal Investigator</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Shantanu Pawar — Department of Mechanical Engineering, PVG's College of Engineering, Technology and Management, Pune, India.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col"><h2 class="label">Profile</h2></div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="section-title">Author of the Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed (VIOT)</h3>
          <div class="prose-block">
            <p>The VIOT research program is a multiscale assessment of carbon-nanomaterial accelerator-grid coatings for charge-exchange (CEX) erosion mitigation in the NASA NSTAR ion thruster.</p>
            <p>Research stack:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Plasma Physics:</strong> GPU PIC-MCC (Particle-in-Cell with Monte Carlo Collisions) simulations.</li>
              <li><strong>Atomistic Modeling:</strong> LAMMPS AIREBO crystalline Molecular Dynamics for ion-surface interactions.</li>
              <li><strong>Computational Engineering:</strong> Custom 3D Poisson solvers and DSMC (Direct Simulation Monte Carlo) pipelines.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col"><h2 class="label">Program Timeline</h2></div>
        <div class="grid-cells cols-3">
          <div>
            <h3>2024</h3>
            <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:0.5rem;line-height:1.5;">Phase I: MATLAB prototype.<br>Phase II: VIOT-2 GPU PIC-MCC prototype.<br>15 defects discovered.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>2025</h3>
            <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:0.5rem;line-height:1.5;">Phase III: VIOT-3 axisymmetric production framework. 70/70 tests pass.<br>Phase IV: VIOT-4 3D + DSMC + MD framework initiated.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>2026</h3>
            <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:0.5rem;line-height:1.5;">Phase V: Consolidated manuscript (35 pages).<br>VIOT-4 core complete.<br>Campaign results finalized.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col">
          <h2 class="label">Documentation</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);line-height:1.5;margin-top:1rem;">17 files<br>Every number, parameter, and algorithm</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="label">Complete research record</p>
          <div class="table-wrap" data-gsap="table">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">01_Project_Overview.md</td><td>Research question, H1–H4, scope, timeline</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">02_Data_Campaign_Results.md</td><td>36 campaign simulations, raw erosion, LEF derivation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">03_Data_EBS_Analysis.md</td><td>10-seed ensemble, barrier physics, LEF_EBS</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">04_Data_Yield_Tables.md</td><td>7 sputter-yield tables, RustBCA + LAMMPS parameters</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">05_Data_Neutral_DSMC.md</td><td>Analytic view factor vs DSMC benchmark, 44.4% deviation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">06_Physics_and_Math.md</td><td>Every governing equation, constant, and derivation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">07_Codebase_VIOT3.md</td><td>Axisymmetric framework: modules, API</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">08_Codebase_VIOT4.md</td><td>3D framework: DSMC, MD pipeline, 3D Poisson</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">09_Verification_and_Tests.md</td><td>70+2 tests, assertions, all results</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">10_Results_Summary.md</td><td>Every headline result with its provenance chain</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">11_Empirical_Reference_Data.md</td><td>NSTAR ELT data, yields, geometries</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">12_Framework_Comparison.md</td><td>VIOT vs. Orbitrap, ONERA</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="td-navy">13-17</td><td>Manuscript history, limitations, reproducibility, references</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col"><h2 class="label">Contact</h2></div>
        <div>
          <p class="prose-block" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Open to collaboration, questions about the research, or opportunities in propulsion and computational physics.</p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn-outline" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Email</a>
            {profile.github && <a class="btn-outline" href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>}
            {profile.linkedin && <a class="btn-outline" href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>}
            {profile.scholar && <a class="btn-outline" href={profile.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>}
            {profile.cv && <a class="btn-outline" href={profile.cv} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CV</a>}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    import gsap from 'gsap';
    import { ScrollTrigger } from 'gsap/ScrollTrigger';
    gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

    if (!window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-gsap="table"]').forEach((table) => {
        const rows = table.querySelectorAll('tbody tr');
        rows.forEach((row, i) => {
          gsap.fromTo(row,
            { opacity: 0, x: -16 },
            { scrollTrigger: { trigger: row, start: 'top 90%' }, opacity: 1, x: 0, duration: 0.4, ease: 'power2.out', delay: i * 0.05 }
          );
        });
      });
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
